            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SYK01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Sykes</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1824-03-27"/>
                    <occupation>dissenting minister</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Godwin often sees him when he is back in East Anglia, sometimes
  specifies Guestwick (in Norfolk), and various websites have a John Sykes as dissenting minister
  at Guestwick at this time.  Godwin records his death on 27 March 1824. 
  http://www.origins.org.uk/genuki/NFK/places/g/guestwick/ has a record of John 
  Alexander's 'sermon, preached in the Independent Meeting-House at Guestwick, April 2, 
  1824, after the internment of J. Sykes' thus the dates clearly fit. The National Archives
  gives Sykes's dates as Independent minister at Guestwick as 1776-1824. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">National Archives.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">http://www.origins.org.uk/genuki/NFK/places/g/guestwick/. </bibl>
                </person>
